# Allow rig.py to shut the system down safely without a password.
#
# In the field there is no SSH and no keyboard, only two buttons. Cutting the
# power during a write can corrupt the file system, so the menu needs a safe
# shutdown entry, and `poweroff` requires root.
#
# The permission is limited to this single command; it does not grant
# password-less sudo in general.
#
# Installed by setup.sh, which replaces __USER__ with the current user and
# validates the file with `visudo -c`. Never skip that check: a syntax error
# in sudoers disables sudo entirely, and then sudo can no longer be used to
# fix it.

__USER__ ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/sbin/poweroff
